{
	"version": 5,
	"id": "B4xF2LOko9Dr10jTm",
	"notes": "A veteran Commissar of the Officio Prefectus: political officer, battlefield disciplinarian, and (per Ciaphas Cain's narration of his own reputation, which he insists is undeserved) supposed to lead from the front and be the last man standing. Point math: ST 11 (+10), DX 12 (+40), IQ 12 (+40), HT 12 (+20) = 110, plus Will +2 (+10) = 120; advantages +51; disadvantages -52; skills +82. Total 201 points, the low end of framework.md's \"Elite human (200-350)\" tier — a senior, experienced Commissar with a long record runs noticeably higher via more Rank and skill points. No psychic abilities here.\n",
	"traits": [
		{
			"id": "tKpXg4_kRp2p5T8bu",
			"name": "ST",
			"local_notes": "Lore: A Commissar is expected to be physically capable, not exceptional.\n\nDesign: ST 11 (+1), 10 pts/level (B15).",
			"tags": [
				"Attribute"
			],
			"base_points": 10,
			"features": [
				{
					"type": "attribute_bonus",
					"attribute": "st",
					"amount": 1
				}
			]
		},
		{
			"id": "tMjskKvH8mEQiNccd",
			"name": "DX",
			"local_notes": "Lore: Trained to a good military standard with both bolt pistol and blade.\n\nDesign: DX 12 (+2), 20 pts/level (B15).",
			"tags": [
				"Attribute"
			],
			"base_points": 40,
			"features": [
				{
					"type": "attribute_bonus",
					"attribute": "dx",
					"amount": 2
				}
			]
		},
		{
			"id": "tjEJmvutKTjVd-g2R",
			"name": "IQ",
			"local_notes": "Lore: Commissars are Schola Progenium or equivalent-trained political officers, not mere disciplinarians.\n\nDesign: IQ 12 (+2), 20 pts/level (B15).",
			"tags": [
				"Attribute"
			],
			"base_points": 40,
			"features": [
				{
					"type": "attribute_bonus",
					"attribute": "iq",
					"amount": 2
				}
			]
		},
		{
			"id": "t1kHLuSMeCF8c_-AF",
			"name": "HT",
			"local_notes": "Lore: A Commissar who leads from the front needs the endurance to survive it.\n\nDesign: HT 12 (+2), 10 pts/level (B14).",
			"tags": [
				"Attribute"
			],
			"base_points": 20,
			"features": [
				{
					"type": "attribute_bonus",
					"attribute": "ht",
					"amount": 2
				}
			]
		},
		{
			"id": "tsYIjD737oIG4ueWZ",
			"name": "Will",
			"local_notes": "Lore: A Commissar's job is to be the one person on the line who does not break — Ciaphas Cain repeatedly notes that whatever else is true of him, his nerve under fire is genuine.\n\nDesign: Will 14 (+2 above IQ-derived default of 12), 5 pts/level (B16).",
			"tags": [
				"Attribute"
			],
			"base_points": 10,
			"features": [
				{
					"type": "attribute_bonus",
					"attribute": "will",
					"amount": 2
				}
			]
		},
		{
			"id": "to_3dcxuwJKtT7qC5",
			"name": "Fearlessness",
			"reference": "B55",
			"local_notes": "Lore: Resolve under fear rather than immunity to it: a Commissar who has ordered executions and watched daemons take a trench line still feels the dread, but holds (Will 14 + 3 = 17 on Fright Checks). Ciaphas Cain's narration is all about mastering fear, not lacking it.\n\nDesign: Basic Set Fearlessness (B55), 2/level, max 5 levels as usual; buy the level that fits the character. Each level adds +1 to Fright Checks; it is the right trait for a Commissar's resolve under fear.",
			"tags": [
				"Advantage",
				"Mental",
				"Imperium"
			],
			"points_per_level": 2,
			"can_level": true,
			"levels": 3
		},
		{
			"id": "tSRncJgUygdmWa5N_",
			"name": "Fit",
			"reference": "B55",
			"local_notes": "Lore: A Commissar who leads from the front keeps himself in condition.\n\nDesign: Basic Set Fit (B55), 5 points.",
			"tags": [
				"Advantage",
				"Physical",
				"Imperium"
			],
			"base_points": 5
		},
		{
			"id": "tC1iDcdVAhEtF2-sC",
			"name": "Combat Reflexes",
			"reference": "B43",
			"local_notes": "Lore: A Commissar cannot afford to freeze; the regiment is watching.\n\nDesign: Basic Set Combat Reflexes (B43), 15 points.",
			"tags": [
				"Advantage",
				"Mental",
				"Imperium"
			],
			"base_points": 15
		},
		{
			"id": "tuWlZeWXvs6on7wPg",
			"name": "Legal Enforcement Powers (Commissariat)",
			"reference": "B65",
			"local_notes": "Lore: A Commissar's authority to enforce discipline within their attached regiment up to and including summary execution for cowardice, desertion, or heresy — a narrower grant than an Inquisitorial rosette (it stops at the regiment's edge) but exercised far more routinely; Ciaphas Cain's narration treats a drawn bolt pistol and the words \"for the Emperor\" as a Commissar's standard response to a wavering line.\n\nDesign: Basic Set Legal Enforcement Powers (B65), 5/level, at 3 levels (15 points) — one tier below an Inquisitorial rosette's maximum, reflecting authority that is real and lethal but scoped to a single command rather than the whole Imperium.",
			"tags": [
				"Advantage",
				"Social",
				"Imperium",
				"Astra Militarum"
			],
			"points_per_level": 5,
			"can_level": true,
			"levels": 3
		},
		{
			"id": "t7H4HsJAgoEYN1mzt",
			"name": "Rank (Officio Prefectus)",
			"reference": "B29",
			"local_notes": "Lore: Commissars hold an officer-equivalent rank within the Officio Prefectus chain, separate from the regiment's own command structure.\n\nDesign: Basic Set Rank (B29), 5/level, 2 levels (10 points), taken as the Commissariat's own hierarchy rather than the regiment's. The Legal Enforcement Powers entry covers the power to enforce discipline; this covers standing within the Officio Prefectus.",
			"tags": [
				"Advantage",
				"Social",
				"Imperium",
				"Astra Militarum"
			],
			"points_per_level": 5,
			"can_level": true,
			"levels": 2
		},
		{
			"id": "Tkf1DEgrRB-yC0qKs",
			"name": "Schola Progenium Origin",
			"local_notes": "Lore: Raised as a ward of the state in the Schola Progenium, the orphanage and academy system that feeds the Commissariat, the Militarum Tempestus and the Sororitas with doctrinally reliable recruits: rote catechism, hard drill, and no family but the institution.\n\nDesign: Net 0 points, two Basic Set perks/quirks. Disabled by default; GM/player enables it. Fills the gap the Scion and Commissar templates leave when they cite Schola upbringing.",
			"tags": [
				"Imperium",
				"Ecclesiarchy"
			],
			"children": [
				{
					"id": "tzQmEWBUHvnYFhFJZ",
					"name": "Schola Catechism",
					"local_notes": "Lore: Years of daily doctrine leave the Creed as second nature.\n\nDesign: Perk (B9), +1 to Theology (Imperial Creed).",
					"tags": [
						"Perk",
						"Imperium"
					],
					"base_points": 1,
					"features": [
						{
							"type": "skill_bonus",
							"selection_type": "skills_with_name",
							"name": {
								"compare": "is",
								"qualifier": "Theology"
							},
							"amount": 1,
							"specialization": {
								"compare": "is",
								"qualifier": "Imperial Creed"
							}
						}
					]
				},
				{
					"id": "tD22cWqRy-W_9GbZ_",
					"name": "Raised as a Ward of the State",
					"local_notes": "Lore: No family, no home world worth the name; the institution was the only parent.\n\nDesign: Quirk (B9), roleplaying flag only.",
					"tags": [
						"Quirk",
						"Imperium"
					],
					"base_points": -1
				}
			],
			"disabled": true
		},
		{
			"id": "tBT8vDeC-yoLFFoaf",
			"name": "Fanaticism (The God-Emperor)",
			"reference": "B136",
			"local_notes": "Lore: A Commissar's authority rests entirely on this belief being genuine, not performed.\n\nDesign: Basic Set Fanaticism (B136), flat -15, taken for \"the Emperor/the Imperial Creed\" as the group/ideal. Not leveled in Basic Set. The Guardsman template carries it disabled: enable it for zealot regiments or characters, and conscript, penal and feral troops leave it off.",
			"tags": [
				"Disadvantage",
				"Mental",
				"Imperium"
			],
			"base_points": -15
		},
		{
			"id": "tMJdZOKze3tm-SRxi",
			"name": "Duty (Astra Militarum)",
			"reference": "B133",
			"local_notes": "Lore: Commissars are themselves Munitorum-bound, answerable to the Officio Prefectus for their conduct.\n\nDesign: Basic Set Duty (B133): almost-always-on-duty, hazardous, involuntary military service, at the top of the disadvantage's standard cost range.",
			"tags": [
				"Disadvantage",
				"Social",
				"Imperium",
				"Astra Militarum"
			],
			"base_points": -15
		},
		{
			"id": "tHSShlX14thdVI0Eh",
			"name": "Intolerance (Heretics)",
			"reference": "B140",
			"local_notes": "Lore: The Commissariat exists specifically to root out heresy, cowardice and defeatism in the ranks.\n\nDesign: Basic Set Intolerance (B140), narrow-category cost (-5).",
			"tags": [
				"Disadvantage",
				"Mental",
				"Imperium"
			],
			"base_points": -5
		},
		{
			"id": "tlcpLNhveJHYLvdHD",
			"name": "Intolerance (Xenos)",
			"reference": "B140",
			"local_notes": "Lore: \"The alien is the enemy\" as baseline Imperial doctrine — not personal bigotry but state religion. Universal across Black Library fiction; only a minority of xenos-sympathetic characters (some Rogue Traders, Ordo Xenos radicals) lack it.\n\nDesign: Basic Set Intolerance (B140). Costed at -10, the \"very broad category\" end of the range the book allows, since \"all non-human sapient species\" is about as broad a target as Intolerance can name.",
			"tags": [
				"Disadvantage",
				"Mental",
				"Imperium"
			],
			"base_points": -10
		},
		{
			"id": "twsVDnObuIR5wIiKZ",
			"name": "Callous",
			"reference": "B125",
			"local_notes": "Lore: The Commissariat's reputation (which Ciaphas Cain's novels explicitly play against, making him an exception) is one of willingness to execute one's own troops without much hesitation.\n\nDesign: Basic Set Callous (B125), -5.",
			"tags": [
				"Disadvantage",
				"Mental",
				"Imperium"
			],
			"base_points": -5
		},
		{
			"id": "tN9oOzvv8qVbghYml",
			"name": "Feared, Not Loved",
			"local_notes": "Lore: Troopers obey a Commissar; they rarely relax around one.\n\nDesign: Quirk (B9), roleplaying flag only.",
			"tags": [
				"Quirk",
				"Imperium"
			],
			"base_points": -1
		},
		{
			"id": "tDD1bSqjZo-7R8sMb",
			"name": "Immaculate Uniform",
			"local_notes": "Lore: Commissarial dress is a deliberate, unmissable symbol of authority and is maintained accordingly, mud and blood permitting.\n\nDesign: Quirk (B9), roleplaying flag only.",
			"tags": [
				"Quirk",
				"Imperium"
			],
			"base_points": -1
		}
	],
